/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,240p' reproduction.md && printf '\\\\n-- problem --\\\\n' && sed -n '1,240p' problem_desc.txt && printf '\\\\n-- task --\\\\n' && cat task.json\""},"result":{"isError":false,"text":"# Public reproduction\n\nRun from the task directory:\n\n```bash\npython reproduce.py\n```\n\nThe command validates the archived session, opens both SpikeGLX streams through\nthe historical project source, loads the registration track in the project's\nnative format, and attempts to materialize the complete corrected AP region.\nIt writes:\n\n```text\noutputs/public_reproduction_report.json\n```\n\nThe report has three lifecycle states:\n\n- `pre_fix_expected_failure`, exit code `1`: the scientific inputs initialized,\n  but the complete workflow did not produce a usable corrected recording;\n- `post_fix_success`, exit code `0`: the complete workflow produced a finite,\n  nontrivial corrected recording with the expected recording structure;\n- `runner_failure`, exit code `2`: the task source, dependency environment, or\n  archived fixture could not be initialized or validated.\n\nThe public command is one real-data smoke case, not the complete correctness\noracle.  A repair must generalize to other valid inputs supported by the\nproject.\n\n-- problem --\nAn electrophysiology group archived the Neuropixels AP and LF streams and the\nregistration track supplied with this task.  The track is used with the LF\nacquisition context to correct a region of the AP recording before downstream\nspike analysis.  All inputs load through the historical SpikeInterface source\nsnapshot, but the complete corrected recording cannot be materialized into a\nscientifically usable result.\n\nRun the offline reproduction, inspect the full source, real acquisition\nmetadata, project manuals, and papers, and repair the implementation so this\nnormal workflow completes.  The repair must preserve the intended physical\nregistration for other valid recordings and registration tracks supported